+# Prior Authorization Request Packet - MRI Lumbar Spine
+
+Synthetic document for DocIntel MVP1 workflow testing. This file contains no real patient information.
+
+## Patient and Encounter
+
+- Patient name: Jordan Taylor
+- Date of birth: 1978-04-18
+- Member ID: DEMO-PA-10021
+- Encounter date: 2026-05-14
+- Ordering provider: Priya Shah, MD
+- Facility: Evergreen Spine and Rehab Clinic
+- Encounter type: outpatient spine evaluation
+
+## Requested Service
+
+- Requested service: MRI lumbar spine without contrast
+- Requested CPT code: 72148
+- Diagnosis: Lumbar radiculopathy
+- ICD-10 code: M54.16
+- Requested urgency: routine
+- Target facility: Cascade Imaging Center
+
+## Clinical History
+
+Jordan Taylor reports low back pain radiating into the left posterior thigh and calf for approximately 9 weeks. Symptoms began after lifting a heavy box at work on 2026-03-10. Pain is worse with prolonged sitting and forward bending. The patient reports intermittent numbness in the left lateral foot.
+
+The patient denies fever, unexplained weight loss, cancer history, recent infection, intravenous drug use, saddle anesthesia, or bowel/bladder dysfunction.
+
+## Physical Exam
+
+- Lumbar range of motion is reduced with flexion.
+- Straight leg raise is positive on the left at 45 degrees.
+- Left ankle reflex is mildly reduced compared with right.
+- Motor strength is 5/5 in bilateral hip flexion, knee extension, ankle dorsiflexion, and great toe extension.
+- Sensation is decreased to light touch over the left lateral foot.
+- Gait is mildly antalgic.
+
+## Conservative Treatment Tried
+
+- NSAID therapy: naproxen 500 mg twice daily from 2026-03-16 to 2026-04-15 with partial temporary relief.
+- Activity modification: avoided lifting over 10 pounds from 2026-03-16 through present.
+- Home exercise program: lumbar stretching and core stabilization from 2026-03-20 through present.
+- Physical therapy: 6 visits from 2026-04-01 to 2026-05-10 focused on McKenzie extension, neural glides, and core stabilization.
+- Outcome: persistent radicular pain rated 7/10 despite conservative treatment.
+
+## Prior Imaging
+
+Lumbar spine X-ray dated 2026-04-05 showed mild degenerative disc disease at L4-L5 and L5-S1 without acute fracture. No prior lumbar MRI is available.
+
+## Provider Assessment and Plan
+
+Assessment: Persistent left lumbar radiculopathy with sensory change and positive straight leg raise after more than 6 weeks of conservative management.
+
+Plan: Order MRI lumbar spine without contrast to evaluate for disc herniation or nerve root compression. Results are expected to guide referral to spine specialist and determine whether epidural steroid injection or surgical consultation should be considered.
+
+Provider signature: Priya Shah, MD
+Signed date: 2026-05-14
+
+## Human Review Notes
+
+This is a synthetic sample. Prior authorization output must be reviewed by a qualified human before payer submission.
